  "body": "Closes #728\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: Opus 5.5 (mac/M1)\nReviewer model: fable-5.1 (mac/M1-r728-fable: REQUEST CHANGES on 1b290ada, APPROVE on ed362e52, the head)\n\n### Problem\nLOT-193 (#734) needs both skins' colours traced to HFR. #1091 captured the default skin (`R728a`), the static stylesheet (`R728b`) and the logo colour; the grey skin's stylesheet was missing, since its `color_key` (`666666/404550/FFFFFF/…`) is only on pages served to a logged-in user1 session.\n\n### How it was captured\n- The operator allowed one logged-in user1 GET (2026-11-18, option 2 on #728): a login and one topic list (`/forum1.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=13`), read only for its `<link rel=stylesheet>` tags.\n- The grey stylesheet was then fetched **without a session** from the URL that page links (`/include/the_style1.php?color_key=666666/…`): the URL alone serves it, so the fixture carries no account data. `R728c` is byte-identical to the raw answer.\n- Before that, a user2 test (operator go relayed on #893): `theme_css_choice` switched to `degrade` and back (page 3 identical before and after) showed that option adds a per-theme stylesheet but does not change the `color_key`.\n\n### What changed\n- `R728c-stylesheet-grey-skin.css` + meta, MANIFEST row, corpus fragment `728-grey-skin.json`.\n- HFR-PROTOCOL.md « Forum stylesheets »: the grey stylesheet is `R728c`; the per-theme `/themes/css/<theme>/style.php` stylesheet (run observation); what gives an account the grey key is **pending capture** (the profile's « Modifier les couleurs du forum », `/setperso.php`, not fetched; follow-up #1096).\n- Not committed, as in #1091: the logo GIF (`#F18F18` stays a run observation; FIXTURES.md has no binary-fixture convention). So `Closes #728` closes the logo criterion with that run observation, knowingly.\n\n### Checks\n- Independent leak check (Sonnet, mac/M1-x728-sonnet, independent of the anonymizer's selectors): CLEAN, no real pseudo of `local.json`, no cookie, token, IP or account identifier; the only e-mail-like string is the anonymizer's known false positive on the image host (#1090).\n- `anonymize.py check --corpus`: 735/735 clean; `unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests`: corpus and MANIFEST agree; `fold.py --check` ok; `swift test` (HFRKit) green; pre-commit green.\n\nAfter the merge: #734 (LOT-193) is told `R728c`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n",
